{
  "$comment": [
    "Which release the updater offers (ReleaseFeed.kt; the Jarvis artifact store is T-0735) and which download URLs it will fetch from.",
    "Read by android-app/app/src/test/.../update/ReleaseFeedTest.kt and the Python mirror android-app/tools/release_feed_test.py.",
    "",
    "Hosts are placeholders, expanded by each test from its own constants, so no real host is written here:",
    "  {gitlab-host}          the build's GitLab (BuildConfig.GITLAB_BASE: a placeholder in unit tests, the house's in CI)",
    "  {github-host}          github.com",
    "  {github-api-host}      api.github.com",
    "  {github-objects-host}  objects.githubusercontent.com",
    "",
    "A feed is the release list as the API returns it (GitHub's `assets` list or GitLab's `assets.links`). `want` is the offer:",
    "versionCode always; versionName, url and notes where given; null when nothing may be offered.",
    "`installed` is the versionCode running now. In `picks`, `prerelease` says whether the user opted in to prereleases (the feed items' own `prerelease` is GitHub's flag).",
    "`newest` cases offer no prerelease. `storedGarbage` is a `raw` list read with its own `adapter`."
  ],

